From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-bandix: traffic monitor only

The app is reduced to the traffic monitor: the totals for LAN and WAN,
the realtime chart (all devices or one, LAN, WAN or both), the device
list with the current rate and the volume for a period, the usage
ranking and the traffic timeline. Removed:

- the Connections and DNS pages (menu entries);
- on the status page: rate limits (global limit, whitelist, schedule
  rules), traffic quotas, the device settings dialog (hostname, limits,
  quota), deleting devices one by one or selected, and the
  Save/Apply/Reset buttons, which do nothing on this page;
- on the settings page: the update check and install, the feedback
  link, the push URLs that send data to a remote endpoint, and the
  connection and DNS sections.

The status page no longer polls the quotas every second and the
schedule rules every five seconds (each call runs the rpcd script and
curl on the router), and no longer asks GitHub for updates each time it
is opened.

rpcd answers only the methods of the monitor (device status, metrics,
ranking, increments, version, clear data, restart); the others return
"Method is disabled in this build". The ACL grants reading the monitor
data and writing only the settings, clear data and restart. Before, the
read part of the ACL also held methods that change data and
installUpdate, which downloaded any URL from the request and installed
it with "apk add --allow-untrusted".

